      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To identify $\\log_3 (27\\sqrt{3})$, we can rewrite 27 and $\\sqrt{3}$ as powers of 3. Specifically, we have\n\\begin{align*}\n27 &= 3^3,\\\\\n\\sqrt{3} &= 3^{1/2}.\n\\end{align*}\nThus,\n\\begin{align*}\n27\\sqrt{3} &= 3^3 \\cdot 3^{1/2} = 3^{3 + 1/2} = 3^{7/2}.\n\\end{align*}\nTherefore,\n\\begin{align*}\n\\log_3 (27\\sqrt{3}) &= \\log_3 (3^{7/2}) = \\frac{7}{2}.\n\\end{align*}\n\nThus, the final answer is $\\boxed{\\frac{7}{2}}$.",
