    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "$\\log_3\\sqrt57=\\frac{\\ln\\sqrt57}{\\ln3}$.\nWe can rewrite $\\sqrt57$ as $5^{\\frac{57}{2}}$:\n$\\log_3\\sqrt57=\\frac{\\ln5^{\\frac{57}{2}}}{\\ln3}=\\frac{\\frac{57}{2}\\ln5}{\\ln3}$.\nWe can rewrite $\\frac{57}{2}\\ln5$ as $28.5\\ln5$:\n$\\log_3\\sqrt57=\\frac{28.5\\ln5}{\\ln3}$.\nWe can simplify the fraction by factoring out $\\frac{3}{2}$ from the numerator:\n$\\log_3\\sqrt57=\\frac{\\frac{3}{2} \\cdot 28.5 \\ln 5}{\\ln 3}$.\nWe know that $\\frac{3}{2} = \\frac{1}{\\ln 3}$, so we can rewrite the equation as:\n$\\log_3\\sqrt57=\\frac{\\frac{1}{\\ln 3} \\cdot 28.5 \\ln 5}{\\ln 3}$.\nWe can cancel out the $\\ln 3$ terms in the numerator and denominator:\n$\\log_3\\sqrt57=\\frac{28.5 \\ln 5}{\\ln 3}$.\nTherefore, $\\log_3\\sqrt57=\\frac{1}{\\boxed{\\ln 3}}$.However, this is not the correct answer. The correct answer is $\\log_3\\sqrt57=\\frac{41}{6}$.",
